Changes were made. This fork adds Android Auto to the original CarPlay project:
hooks in SAL around the Android Auto receiver library (a cluster video sink, the
input source a display needs, a navigation status service, the rewritten service
discovery response, protocol 1.7 navigation), the "decode mode" that decodes the
phone's cluster stream on the head unit through a second mm-renderer context into a
Screen window on the cluster source display so that the stock encoder sends it, the
HMI counterpart that keeps the cluster's "navigation on the mobile device" notice away
during Android Auto, a diagnostic capture of the phone's stream, a release and an
expert Green Engineering Menu, and the verification on firmware MST2_EU_SK_ZR_P0478T.

